<title>JAPAN: Japan Oct rubber imports rise 16.7 pct year/year.</title>
<headline>Japan Oct rubber imports rise 16.7 pct year/year.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's rubber imports in October totalled 69,922 tonnes, up 16.7 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Thursday showed.</p>
<p>Figures were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			Oct 96	Sept 96	Oct 95</p>
<p> Total		69,922	61,012	 59,907</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Thailand	   50,705	42,404	 43,667</p>
<p> Indonesia	  13,957	 9,862	  9,773</p>
<p> Malaysia	    3,951	 7,625	  5,318</p>
<p>Imports in the first 10 months of 1996 were 608,275 tonnes, against 571,791 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (81-3-3432-7431)</p>
